//! The `finalize_spawn` hooks and helpers: declarations the mod API generator reads (see `hooks/mod.rs`).

pub trait Hooks {
    /// NeoForge's `FinalizeSpawnEvent`: the unspawned mob of type `kind` is at `pos`. Where vanilla calls `Mob.finalizeSpawn` (equipment, attributes, variants and class setup), this event precedes it. Monster spawner blocks, spawner minecarts and trial spawners also post this event for configured NBT; they lend the loaded mob and still skip vanilla finalization for those attempts. `spawner` is `Spawner::Block` for a monster spawner block (`SpawnerBlockEntity`), `Spawner::Trial` for a trial spawner block (`TrialSpawnerBlockEntity`), `Spawner::Minecart` for a spawner minecart (`MinecartSpawner`), or `None` otherwise (`FinalizeSpawnEvent.getSpawner`). A minecart handle reads the current cart state through the supplied read-only host. `difficulty` is the local difficulty finalization reads: change it to change what the mob gets. There are two cancels. Return `Flow::Cancel` to skip finalization: no finalizeSpawn runs, and the mob still spawns, without vanilla finalization (configured data and the spawner’s separate equipment table are not finalization). Set `spawn_cancelled` to stop the spawn: no mob is added; on spawners, vanilla finalization (when unconfigured and not skipped with `Flow::Cancel`), trial persistence and any configured equipment table roll still run before `spawn_cancelled` vetoes admission (matching NeoForge's `EventHooks.finalizeMobSpawnSpawner`, `BaseSpawner.serverTick`, `TrialSpawner.spawnMob` and `NeoForgeEventHandler.builtinMobSpawnBlocker`), while outside spawners finalization does not run. It draws nothing itself; skipped finalization skips its draws, and with no listener or an untouched event the draws are vanilla's. Outside spawners, fired only where vanilla 26.3 calls `finalizeSpawn` on a mob the game makes, with vanilla's `reason` at that call: natural spawning, chunk generation's animals, spawners, trial spawners, patrols, raids and sieges, zombie reinforcements, a cat spawner's cat, phantoms, jockeys, `/summon` and `/raid`, spawn eggs and dispensers, the nether portal's piglin (`Structure`), a skeleton trap's horse and riders, an evoker's vexes and wandering traders. A conversion fires with `Conversion`, and a cancel there leaves the converted mob as it is. Not fired where vanilla creates the mob without `finalizeSpawn`: breeding and a baby from a spawn egg, an infested block's or effect's silverfish, a thrown egg's chick, a thrown pearl's endermite, a hatching egg's turtle, sniffer or tadpole, a copper golem built from blocks, a slime from the oozing effect and a lightning trap's horse. Nor for entities loaded from disk or structure mobs placed by world generation. `mob` is a scoped [`UnspawnedMobEditor`] borrowing the mob itself, not yet in a level: read it directly (`event.mob.kind()`, `event.mob.equipment(slot)`, `event.mob.attribute_base(id)`) and change it directly (`event.mob.set_equipment(slot, item)`, `event.mob.set_attribute_base(id, base)`, tags and the custom name) without passing `host`. The loan lasts only for this hook call; the ender dragon (kept apart from mobs) answers its `kind` and `position` and `Unsupported` for the rest. Listeners run before finalization: finalization's own rolls (equipment, attribute bonuses, variants) still run after them and overwrite what a listener put in the same slot or attribute; `Flow::Cancel` keeps every edit, since no finalization follows. A mob finalization itself makes (a chicken jockey's chicken, a zombie horse's rider) gets its own stack loan. `group` is the pack's spawn group data (`SpawnGroupData`, `SpawnGroup`): what the listener leaves there is what finalization reads for this mob. Chunk generation threads it through the pack; live spawning does not yet thread group data through its packs. The host is the read-only one, and `event.mob` changes nothing but this mob: listeners run on replayed ticks, so they must be pure functions of their inputs and edit only `mob` and `group`. Server-side.
    #[notes = r#"## Finalize spawn

- **`finalize_spawn(dimension, kind, reason, pos, spawner, difficulty, spawn_cancelled, mob, group, cancel)`** (NeoForge's `FinalizeSpawnEvent`, version 3): fires before `Mob.finalizeSpawn`, and also for configured spawner NBT even though vanilla finalization will not run. There are two cancels: return `Flow::Cancel` to skip finalization (the mob still spawns, and only finalization’s rolls and setup are skipped), or set `spawn_cancelled` so no mob is added. `difficulty` (`Difficulty`) is settable and is what finalization reads. `spawner` is `Spawner::Block` for a monster spawner block, `Spawner::Trial` for a trial spawner block, `Spawner::Minecart` for a spawner minecart, or `None` otherwise (`FinalizeSpawnEvent.getSpawner`). A minecart handle reads the current cart state through the supplied read-only host. Outside spawners, fired only where vanilla 26.3 calls `finalizeSpawn`, with vanilla's reason at that call: natural spawning, chunk generation, spawners, trial spawners, patrols, raids and sieges, reinforcements, cat spawners, phantoms, jockeys, `/summon`, `/raid`, spawn eggs, dispensers, the nether portal's piglin (`Structure`), skeleton traps, evoker vexes, wandering traders and conversions. Not fired where vanilla creates the mob without it (breeding, an infested block's silverfish, a thrown egg's chick, a thrown pearl's endermite, hatching eggs, built golems, the oozing effect's slimes, a lightning trap's horse), for loads (`persist.rs` finalizes a placed entity only through its `sunrise:finalize` marker, which is a load) or for structure mobs placed by world generation. The mob being finalized is lent directly on the stack as `event.mob` (`UnspawnedMobEditor<'_>`): read it directly without `host` (`kind`, `position`, `equipment`, `attribute_base`, `attribute_value`, `tags`, `custom_name`) and edit it directly (`set_equipment`, `set_attribute_base`, `add_attribute_modifier`, `remove_attribute_modifier`, `add_tag`, `remove_tag`, `set_custom_name`). Each edit applies at once and reaches only that mob; the borrow cannot outlive the hook call, so there is no handle or `Expired` state. The editor is a scoped loan rather than a `&mut dyn ServerHost` because the hook fires inside spawning passes that hold the level shared (natural spawning, spawners), as `CriterionContext` is lent to a criterion test. Listeners run before finalization, so finalization's own equipment and attribute rolls overwrite a listener's edit to the same slot or attribute; `Flow::Cancel` keeps every edit. Mobs that finalization creates (jockeys, a zombie horse's rider) get a stack loan of their own. The ender dragon, kept apart from mobs, answers its `kind` and `position` and `Unsupported` for the rest. `group` (`&mut Option<SpawnGroup>`) is the pack's `SpawnGroupData`, converted at the boundary: the listener may read, change, set or clear it, and finalization reads what it leaves. Chunk generation passes group data to the next pack member; live spawning does not yet thread it through packs. The new types are plain data (`Difficulty`, `Spawner`, `SpawnGroup`, `AgeableGroup`, `TropicalVariant`, `#[non_exhaustive]`). Read-only host; listeners run on replayed ticks, so they are pure functions of their inputs and change only `event.mob` and `group`. Tick-time effect: one `listened` branch with no listeners; with one, a direct stack borrow with no copy or arena entry. Beyond NeoForge: none.

`window_resize` notifies client mods after a window resize or applying a changed GUI scale, fullscreen, or Unicode font setting. Its `width` and `height` are physical pixels, and `gui_width` and `gui_height` are scaled GUI pixels. It fires only when physical or scaled dimensions change.

### Structure template reads

`LevelRef::visit_structure_template(host, id, at, rotation, mirror, visit)` reads a template
without placing it. It searches the world's saved templates before data packs, lends each
transformed block as a `StructureTemplateBlockView<'_>` in vanilla placement order with its
transformed state and borrowed block-entity data (stopping early on `ControlFlow::Break(())`),
and returns the rotated size `[i32; 3]`. It uses the palette selected at `at`; processors and
entities are not included. Refusals return a typed `StructureTemplateError`. A builder can read
the template and place its blocks over time."#]
    #[hook(
        receiver = "read",
        dispatch = "api_carrier",
        side = "server",
        contract = "cancel",
        out = "cancel",
        host = "read",
        neoforge = "FinalizeSpawnEvent",
        cancellable = true,
        version = 3
    )]
    fn finalize_spawn(
        dimension: &str,
        kind: &str,
        reason: SpawnReason,
        pos: [f64; 3],
        spawner: Option<Spawner>,
        difficulty: &mut Difficulty,
        spawn_cancelled: &mut bool,
        mob: UnspawnedMobEditor<'_>,
        group: &mut Option<SpawnGroup>,
        cancel: &mut bool,
    );
}
